# The tenth tooling step's pull request of the owner's decisions of
# 2026-11-16.

# A managed `ask` holds back the user's own check.

[break] managed-ask-is-not-marked
rule: A finding an `ask` rule of the managed configuration makes says so, and the question carries it.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/engine.rs
in: Finding::asked_by
find: managed: matches!(hit.by, By::Rule(rule) if rule.source == RuleSource::Managed)
replace: managed: false
packages: cortex-policy, cortex-core
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it verify::a_users_check_a_managed_ask_rule_asks_about_does_not_run_and_a_users_own_ask_does

[break] managed-ask-lets-the-users-line-run
rule: The verifier holds back the user's own line where a managed `ask` rule is among what asks.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/verify.rs
find: Decision::Ask if managed =>
replace: Decision::Ask if managed && false =>
caught-by:
    verify::a_users_check_a_managed_ask_rule_asks_about_does_not_run_and_a_users_own_ask_does

[break] any-ask-holds-the-users-line-back
rule: A user's own `ask` rule does not hold back the user's own line: only the managed configuration's does.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/engine.rs
in: Finding::asked_by
find: matches!(hit.by, By::Rule(rule) if rule.source == RuleSource::Managed)
replace: matches!(hit.by, By::Rule(_))
packages: cortex-policy, cortex-core
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it verify::a_users_check_a_managed_ask_rule_asks_about_does_not_run_and_a_users_own_ask_does

[break] managed-ask-loses-a-tie
rule: Of rules of one strength the managed configuration's is the hit, so a managed `ask` beside another layer's `ask` on the same call is still marked.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/rules.rs
in: RuleSet::strongest
find: compiled.rule.source == RuleSource::Managed
replace: false
caught-by:
    managed_ask::a_managed_ask_is_marked_beside_another_layers_ask_in_either_order

[break] managed-ask-on-a-named-path-is-not-marked
rule: A managed rule's `ask` on a path a command only names is marked.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/engine.rs
in: Engine::judge_named_path
find: By::Rule(_) => Finding::asked_by(reason, &hit)
replace: By::Rule(_) => Finding::ask(reason)
caught-by:
    managed_ask::an_ask_of_the_managed_configuration_is_marked_whichever_way_it_comes

[break] managed-ask-on-a-path-is-not-marked
rule: A managed rule's `ask` on a path a call reads or writes is marked.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/engine.rs
in: Engine::judge_path
find: Finding::asked_by(format!("{what} is asked about by {}.", hit.describe()), &hit)
replace: Finding::ask(format!("{what} is asked about by {}.", hit.describe()))
caught-by:
    managed_ask::an_ask_of_the_managed_configuration_is_marked_whichever_way_it_comes

[break] managed-ask-is-forgotten-by-a-later-reason
rule: A question is managed when any of its reasons is a managed rule's, whatever comes after it.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/engine.rs
find: managed |= by_managed;
replace: managed = by_managed;
caught-by:
    managed_ask::an_ask_of_the_managed_configuration_is_marked_whichever_way_it_comes
